#: ../../source/docs/learning-ardupilot-threading.rst:10
#: f11b3d9599354b3b91567be7ff827fb2
msgid "Once you have learned the basic of the ArduPilot libraries it is time for you to understand how ArduPilot deals with threading. The setup()/loop() structure that was inherited from arduino may make it seem that ArduPilot is a single threaded system, but in fact it isn't."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/learning-ardupilot-threading.rst:15
#: e4f660fac6ef4c97a2ad12442bfd1e2b
msgid "The threading approach in ArduPilot depends on the board it is built for. Some boards (such as the APM1 and APM2) don't support threads, so make do with a simple timer and callbacks. Some boards (PX4 and Linux) support a rich Posix threading model with realtime priorities, and these are used extensively by ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/learning-ardupilot-threading.rst:21
#: dbf9d817ca3a4c3babb688ffbed8a9dd
msgid "There are a number of key concepts related to threading that you need to understand in ArduPilot:"
msgstr ""

